## Context

Child of 0700. Backward and forward citation search from the ICF works retained
by 1655. Decision of the 29 September consultation: two rounds; a third only if
the second brings admissible works. Rerun conditions: interrupted query, missed
sentinel, external reference without decision, incomplete summary.

Baseline integration closes under 1655. This ticket owns incremental delivery,
pool merge, ICF screening, venue and discipline refresh, and count reconciliation
for its additions, through the existing intake and screening procedures. Screen
each round before measuring its eligible yield and choosing the next frontier.
Keep uncertain works and sentinel routes in the seed roster; the fully graded
REL set alone is not the discovery universe. Execution plan and baseline evidence:
`docs/rel-corpus-completion-2026-10-08.md`.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Two rounds run, counts per round (references and citations, duplicates, new works)
- [ ] Third round triggered or dropped, with the measurement that decides it
- [ ] New works delivered under the intake contract with provenance, merged and screened incrementally within 1654; venue/discipline data and counts reconciled before each round's yield is measured

## Raid checkpoint — 1654 — Phase 2 Imagine

The baseline is complete but chaining has not run. Simplest path: a narrow resumable OpenAlex collector plus existing intake/pool/screen/venue/view procedures. Discovery seeds are final ICF icf/unsure and sentinels, not the fully graded REL population: baseline 19,852 seeds, 17,641 OA identities, 2,211 missing OA identities, 6,433 without DOI. Resolve missing IDs or document unresolved routes. Do not replace this discovery population with 7,499 inclusions. Avoid a new harvest framework. Existing metadata resolvers are lossy and existing cursor search is not resumable; reuse HTTP/text/keystore helpers, not their filtered outputs. Archive complete raw payloads and separate seed–candidate edges.

